[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"MongoDB Aggregation Pipeline Stages: $match, $project, $group, $unwind, $sort, $limit, $skip"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"The MongoDB aggregation pipeline is a powerful framework for data processing and transformation. It consists of a sequence of stages, each performing a specific operation on the input documents. This tutorial covers the essential stages: $match, $project, $group, $unwind, $sort, $limit, and $skip."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"$match: Filtering Documents"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"The '$match' stage filters the documents to pass only the documents that match the specified condition(s) to the next pipeline stage. It's analogous to the 'WHERE' clause in SQL."},{"order":5,"type":"code","text":"db.collection.aggregate([
  { $match: { status: "A" } }
])"},{"order":6,"type":"paragraph","text":"This example filters the 'collection' to only include documents where the 'status' field is equal to "A"."},{"order":7,"type":"subheading","text":"$project: Reshaping Documents"},{"order":8,"type":"paragraph","text":"The '$project' stage reshapes each document in the stream, such as adding new fields or removing existing fields. It's similar to the 'SELECT' clause in SQL."},{"order":9,"type":"code","text":"db.collection.aggregate([
  { $project: { _id: 0, name: 1, status: 1 } }
])"},{"order":10,"type":"paragraph","text":"This example projects only the 'name' and 'status' fields, and excludes the '_id' field from the output documents. Setting a field to '1' includes it, and setting it to '0' excludes it."},{"order":11,"type":"subheading","text":"$group: Grouping Documents"},{"order":12,"type":"paragraph","text":"The '$group' stage groups documents by a specified key and performs aggregation operations (e.g., sum, average, count) on the grouped documents. It's similar to the 'GROUP BY' clause in SQL."},{"order":13,"type":"code","text":"db.collection.aggregate([
  { $group: { _id: "$status", total: { $sum: 1 } } }
])"},{"order":14,"type":"paragraph","text":"This example groups documents by the 'status' field and calculates the total count of documents for each status. The '$sum: 1' operator increments the count by 1 for each document in the group."},{"order":15,"type":"subheading","text":"$unwind: Deconstructing Array Fields"},{"order":16,"type":"paragraph","text":"The '$unwind' stage deconstructs an array field in the input documents to output a document for each element of the array. This is useful for processing array data."},{"order":17,"type":"code","text":"db.collection.aggregate([
  { $unwind: "$sizes" }
])"},{"order":18,"type":"paragraph","text":"If a document has a 'sizes' array field, this example will create a new document for each element in the 'sizes' array."},{"order":19,"type":"subheading","text":"$sort: Sorting Documents"},{"order":20,"type":"paragraph","text":"The '$sort' stage sorts the documents based on specified field(s) in ascending or descending order. It's similar to the 'ORDER BY' clause in SQL."},{"order":21,"type":"code","text":"db.collection.aggregate([
  { $sort: { age: -1 } }
])"},{"order":22,"type":"paragraph","text":"This example sorts the documents in descending order based on the 'age' field. Use '1' for ascending order and '-1' for descending order."},{"order":23,"type":"subheading","text":"$limit: Limiting Results"},{"order":24,"type":"paragraph","text":"The '$limit' stage limits the number of documents passed to the next stage. It's similar to the 'LIMIT' clause in SQL."},{"order":25,"type":"code","text":"db.collection.aggregate([
  { $limit: 10 }
])"},{"order":26,"type":"paragraph","text":"This example limits the output to the first 10 documents."},{"order":27,"type":"subheading","text":"$skip: Skipping Documents"},{"order":28,"type":"paragraph","text":"The '$skip' stage skips a specified number of documents before passing the remaining documents to the next stage. It's often used for pagination."},{"order":29,"type":"code","text":"db.collection.aggregate([
  { $skip: 5 }
])"},{"order":30,"type":"paragraph","text":"This example skips the first 5 documents and passes the rest to the next stage."},{"order":31,"type":"subheading","text":"Combining Stages"},{"order":32,"type":"paragraph","text":"These stages can be combined to create complex data processing pipelines. The order of stages can significantly impact performance and results. It's generally recommended to filter data as early as possible using '$match' to reduce the amount of data processed by subsequent stages."},{"order":33,"type":"code","text":"db.collection.aggregate([
  { $match: { status: "A" } },
  { $group: { _id: "$city", total: { $sum: 1 } } },
  { $sort: { total: -1 } },
  { $limit: 5 }
])"},{"order":34,"type":"paragraph","text":"This example first filters documents with 'status' equal to "A", then groups them by 'city' to count the total documents per city, sorts the results by the total count in descending order, and finally limits the output to the top 5 cities."}]
